:"s:SZ","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"SignedInteger"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Takes the canonical minimum spanning tree (weight, then position, as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"minimumSpanningTree(weight:)"},{"type":"text","text":"), a minimum-weight perfect matching on its odd-degree"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertices ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"minimumWeightMatching"},{"type":"text","text":"), and an Eulerian circuit of their union by Hierholzer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from the first vertex, shortcut to the first visit of each vertex. The matching is on the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"complete graph of the odd vertices in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" order (pairs i < j lexicographic), and the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"circuit’s multigraph lists the tree edges by position, then the matched pairs in that order,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"so the tour is determined. At most 3\/2 × the shortest tour when the weights satisfy the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"triangle inequality (not checked)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Tours read the simple graph, as ","type":"text"},{"code":"nearestNeighborTour(weight:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" documents; nil below three","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertices.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"aside","style":"note","name":"Precondition","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The graph is complete; the sum along a tour fits in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"W"},{"type":"text","text":". When "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"W"},{"type":"text","text":" is a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FixedWidthInteger"},{"type":"text","text":", every non-loop edge’s weight satisfies n · (2 · |weight| + 1) ≤"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"W.max \/ 8"},{"type":"text","text":" (the matching’s bound), checked as each weight is read, so a weight beyond it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"traps even on an edge the matching never sees; so n ≤ "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"W.max \/ 8"},{"type":"text","text":" (15 vertices for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int8"},{"type":"text","text":"), whatever the weights. An arbitrary-precision integer has no bound."}]}]},{"type":"aside","style":"note","name":"Complexity","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"O(n³): the matching on up to n vertices; the tree O(n²)."}]}]}]}],"kind":"symbol","variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/tours\/graphprotocols\/graph\/christofidestour(weight:)-6qvc8"]}],"metadata":{"extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","role":"symbol","externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5ToursE16christofidesTour6weight5Walks5CycleVy6VertexQz5Edges_5IndexQZGSgqd__ANXE_tSZRd__lF","roleHeading":"Instance Method","modules":[{"name":"Tours","relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"]}],"title":"christofidesTour(weight:)","remoteSource":{"fileName":"Christofides.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Tours\/Christofides.swift#L140"},"symbolKind":"method","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"christofidesTour","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"weight","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": (","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Edges","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text"